---
layout: layout.njk
pagination:
  data: events
  size: 1
  alias: event
  # Task 10 (phase 5) established this flag for event.njk, for the
  # identical reason it is needed here: without it, Eleventy adds only the
  # *first* page a paginated template generates to `collections.all`, and
  # `sitemap.njk`'s own loop over that collection would list one survey
  # page, not one per edition.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
# D-19: `event_id` IS `edition_code`, lower-cased -- nothing else names an
# event, the identical rule `event.njk`'s own permalink already applies,
# and the one `tools/convener_ops/survey_invite.SURVEY_BASE`/`survey_url` must
# agree with (pinned by `tools/tests/test_workflows.py::
# test_survey_base_matches_the_survey_page_permalink`).
permalink: "/survey/{{ event.id | lower }}/"
# Excluded from the sitemap (site/sitemap.njk) -- see that template's own
# comment for the pattern this follows, the same choice it already makes
# for the two archive facets. This page is reached exactly one way: a
# link in `tools/convener_ops/survey_invite.py`'s own e-mail, sent after the
# event to people this project already has a reason to write to. A search
# engine sending a stranger here gains that stranger nothing -- the page
# answers no question anyone would search for, and a survey it has no
# invitation for reads as 'not open' regardless. Still fully reachable at
# its own real address for anyone who does hold the link; this flag
# decides only what a crawler is pointed at.
sitemap: false
eleventyComputed:
  pageTitle: "Survey — {{ event.title }}"
  pageDescription: "A short, optional post-event survey for {{ event.title }}."
---

{#
  Phase 7 task 5: the post-event survey's own static page, one per event
  (D-19), the same per-event addressing `event.njk` already uses for
  registration -- this is *why* that page is the closer mechanical
  analogue, even though this page's own layout (a dedicated hero plus one
  section, nothing else on it) reads closer to `verify.njk`: unlike
  registration, which is one form among several bands on an edition's own
  page, the survey has never lived there -- it is reached only from a
  link in an e-mail (`tools/convener_ops/survey_invite.py`), sent after the
  event, to people this project has no other reason to send back to the
  event page itself.

  Before this task, `/survey/<event id>` lived inside the operators'
  own application bundle (`App.tsx`'s former `SurveyRoute`) -- the one
  asymmetry the security audit's web surface review named: registration
  and certificate verification were both already extracted (D-18); the
  survey was not. This page, and the island it mounts
  (`app/src/islands/survey/`), close that gap.
#}

<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero__inner">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Post-event survey</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">What did you think?</h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      A short, optional survey for {{ event.title }}. Three questions, all short.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section container survey-page">
  <p class="event-lead__back">
    <a href="{{ ('/events/' ~ (event.id | lower) ~ '/') | url }}" class="unstyled">&larr; {{ event.title }}</a>
  </p>

  {#
    Phase 4 spec S:6, the wording `app/src/survey/SurveyForm.tsx::Notice`
    used to carry before this task (quoted here unchanged, not redrafted)
    -- moved to plain static HTML ahead of this island's own mount point,
    the identical D-18 move task 6 made for registration's own notice on
    `event.njk`. `tools/tests/test_site.py` pins the ordering, the
    retention figure and the anonymity claim against this copy now,
    the same way it already pins `event.njk`'s.
  #}
  <div class="notice">
    <p class="notice__eyebrow">Before you answer</p>
    <p>
      This short, optional survey is only sent to people we have recorded as present at
      this event. Three questions, all short.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your browser encrypts your answers before they are sent</strong>, using
      this event&rsquo;s own key &mdash; the same key, and the same protection, as your
      registration. Nobody &mdash; including us &mdash; can read your answers until a
      workshop organiser decrypts them as part of running the event.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Your answers are anonymous.</strong> Nothing here &mdash; no name, no
      address, no matching code &mdash; is sent alongside them, and that is deliberate.
      Because of that, we cannot find your own answers to show them to you, correct them
      or erase them individually once sent: there is nothing on file that says which
      answers are yours. Please do not write your name, your email address, or anything
      else that could identify you or anyone else, in the free-text box below.
    </p>
    <p>
      All answers for this event, like your registration, are permanently destroyed
      together with the event&rsquo;s key 90 days after the event. Questions about this
      survey can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  {#
    The survey island itself, mounted here -- extracted from the
    operators' application into its own small, self-contained bundle
    (`app/src/islands/survey/`), the same move task 6 made for
    registration and task 7 made for certificate verification. A
    participant answering this survey never downloads the operators'
    cockpit to do it.

    `#survey-form` is `app/src/islands/survey/main.tsx`'s own `MOUNT_ID`.
    `data-event-id` is how the island learns which event it is on: one
    static page per event (D-19), not a route param this script
    re-parses. The element starts empty; `survey.js` fills it in, which
    is exactly why the `<noscript>` fallback beside it exists -- without
    JavaScript, nothing here would ever render at all.
  #}
  <div id="survey-form" data-event-id="{{ event.id | lower }}"></div>
  <noscript>
    <p class="notice">
      Answering this survey needs JavaScript enabled. If you cannot enable it, write to
      <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a> and we
      will note your feedback by hand.
    </p>
  </noscript>
  <script type="module" src="{{ '/app/islands/survey/survey.js' | url }}"></script>
</section>
